[Music]  hi  thank you for coming here in time and  agreeing to answer my 21 questions  and bringing me to your students house  today  well what did you have for breakfast  this morning  well i had to pour an all-nighter  yesterday because of my baby boy so  i just had instant noodles with bamboo  shoots  how do you usually travel to school i  travel to school on my scooter  which has been my means of  transportation for over six years  how long is your journey to school from  door to door  it's about five kilometer  yes that's not too far what's your  mindset when you enter the school  building every day  uh i just asked myself the question what  will the kids  learn from me today great  name one thing you love about the area  your school is in  uh that is about people who are ethnic  minority people  that's very honest kind and  hospitable yes i see who's your favorite  movie star  angelina jolie you know she is really  amazing  who's your favorite singer or your  favorite band  uh i am a devout fan of taylor swift  i really love her way she overcomes  difficulties in life  and challenges to succeed who's your  hero  my mom she is not only a mother  but a teacher a friend and a doctor  you are so lucky what's the one place  you would love to visit england that is  because  i'm teaching english so i really want to  experience  what i have learned and what i have  taught  from the textbook about people and  culture  and you know i love the culture which is  called  like uh safe uplift  what was your favorite subject in school  um english absolutely  the language i'm teaching now  i see what was your least favorite  subject at school  chemistry actually i was  very bad at chemistry what  i can remember about this subject is  that  what it consists of hydrogen and oxygen  what kind of student were you at school  a kind of  book one i was a very good student  without any boyfriend  what's your favorite food in the school  cafeteria  well in our school we do not have  cafeteria  but sometimes my students often bring  the specialties in the village and i do  love  seven color sticky rice which is made  from the different kinds of leaves in  the mountain  uh you know the surrounding mountains  here  what time do you usually leave school at  the end of the day  about 5 30 pm then i go back to my house  to take care of my baby boy  and i'm typically the first people to  come  to my school and the last to leave  do you usually keep working when you get  home  yep always wow you are hard working  what what do you do to relax well  playing with my little boy and swim in  the waterfall  somewhere very near here and you know  it's fantastic  what are your passions or hobbies  outside teaching  listening to music and reading  what's your proudest achievement as a  teacher  well that is not my prizes and  awards the proudest  achievement is that we are substantially  moving the learning barriers for ethnic  minorities  in the remote area then you know so far  we have  traveled over 40 countries so far  if you could write one motivational  quote on your blackboard  what would it be well  life have two rules number one  never give up number two remember number  one  that is my favorite quotation  what's the most important advice you  would give to your students  education is the most powerful weapon  for changing the world  and finally my last question why did you  become a teacher  when i was a little kid my mom brought  me to the village hall  to watch a movie named the mountainous  school  and the movie really sparked in me an  interest  to become the teacher that is because i  know the difficulties of poor educated  people and i really don't want them  to be kidnapped by a young man to be his  wife  or to be any uh kind of victims of  social evil  or any evil customs so for me  education is like the best channel  to change the world here so i really  want to become a teacher  wow that's such an inspirational story  thank you so much for answering my 21  questions

